Done. One small, concrete improvement committed (`a9dd03d`).

**The fix**: `parse_status_files` (src/git.rs) — the parser behind `/git stage` — treated porcelain rename lines (`R  old_name.rs -> new_name.rs`) as a single filename `"old_name.rs -> new_name.rs"`, so staging in a repo with renames would run `git add "old -> new"` and fail. It now splits on `" -> "` (via `rsplit_once` so filenames containing `" -> "` still resolve) and returns the target path.

**Regression tests added**:
• `test_parse_status_files_rename` — rename + copy lines resolve to the new filename
• `test_parse_status_files_utf8_filename` — multi-byte filenames round-trip without byte-slice panics

**Verification**: `cargo fmt` ✓, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` ✓, `cargo build` ✓, `cargo test` ✓ (4381 passed, 2 ignored). The commit also swept a pre-existing `tools/gasp-emit/Cargo.lock` dependency-resolution change left by an earlier build.
